# Upstream pins for displayif's vendored code and its other build inputs.
#
# displayif is source-integrated: it has no versioned releases of its own
# (see README "Status"). This file records what a build is tested against
# and where the one vendored third-party source tree came from.

## MicroPython
The MicroPython this module builds against is the one pinned for the whole
repository, in ../../UPSTREAM (a full commit; provenance.json names it in words).
CI builds the unix port from that pin. Nothing here repeats it, so it can't go stale.
  Verify locally with: git -C <your micropython checkout> rev-parse HEAD   # matches ../../UPSTREAM

## CircuitPython (usdl2 desktop path only, as a user C module)
Tested against: 11.0.0-alpha.2 (CircuitPython 11 is the first line whose
USER_C_MODULES block matches MicroPython 1.29's)
  https://github.com/adafruit/circuitpython @ d53b2277c

## SDL2 (desktop usdl2 backend)
Minimum: >= 2.0 (SDL_* API used by src/ports/desktop/usdl2/)
Tested locally against: 2.30.0 (`pkg-config --modversion sdl2`)
CI installs Ubuntu's `libsdl2-dev` package (see ../../.github/workflows/displayif.yml).

## Protomatter (vendored, src/ports/common/rgbmatrix/protomatter/)
Vendored from https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit_Protomatter (BSD).
Identified upstream revision: tag 1.7.1, commit
  629d5007f0dfeba244ae81759ce2ba568224cd8a
core.c and core.h are byte-identical to that revision once whitespace/
formatting is normalized (pointer-spacing and brace style differ only;
no logic differences). See src/ports/common/rgbmatrix/protomatter/README.md
for how this was verified and what is not yet known (exact import date,
whether arch/*.h received the same local reformatting).
